.TH NFC-POLL 1 "2026-06-27" "libnci 1.0.0-alpha.1" "libnci manual"
.SH NAME
nfc-poll \- detect NFC tags and print their type and UID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nfc-poll
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nfc-poll
starts RF discovery on an NCI controller (PN7160 by default) and prints the
protocol, UID and basic attributes of every tag brought into the field. When
several tags are present at once it cycles through them. It exercises the
generic
.I nci_*
API: selective technology polling, multi-tag selection and structured errors.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --chipset " NAME"
Controller driver to use (default: the autoprobed default).
.TP
.BI --tech " ABFV"
Restrict polling to the given technologies; any subset of
.BR A ", " B ", " F ", " V
(default: all).
.TP
.B --list
List the compiled-in chipset drivers and exit.
.TP
.BI --bus " PATH"
I2C bus device node (default: /dev/i2c-1).
.TP
.BI --addr " HEX"
I2C address of the controller (default: 0x28).
.TP
.BI --chip " PATH"
GPIO chip device node; autodetected when omitted.
.TP
.BI --ven " N" ", " --irq " N" ", " --dwl " N"
GPIO line offsets for the VEN (reset), IRQ (data-ready) and DWL
(firmware-download) signals.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NCI_LOG
Log verbosity 0\(en5 (silent, error, warn, info, NCI frames, raw bytes).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on a clean exit (Ctrl-C), non-zero if the device could not be opened or
discovery failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nfc-poll
nfc-poll --tech A --list
NCI_LOG=4 nfc-poll
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nfc-detect (1),
.BR nfc-read-ndef (1),
.BR nfc-write-ndef (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the libnci NFC stack.
